To configure Clerk webhooks for your local development environment, you'll need a **public URL** that forwards requests to your local Express server. The easiest way is using **ngrok**.

## Step 1: Install ngrok

Download from:

[ngrok Downloads](https://ngrok.com/download?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Or install via npm:

```bash
npm install -g ngrok
```

---

## Step 2: Start Your Backend

If your Express server runs on:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

start it:

```bash
npm run dev
```

---

## Step 3: Start ngrok

Open a new terminal:

```bash
ngrok http 5000
```

You'll get something like:

```text
Forwarding
https://abc123.ngrok-free.app -> http://localhost:5000
```

Copy the HTTPS URL.

---

## Step 4: Create Clerk Webhook

Go to:

[Clerk Dashboard](https://dashboard.clerk.com?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Navigate:

```text
Configure
   ↓
Webhooks
   ↓
Add Endpoint
```

Endpoint URL:

```text
https://abc123.ngrok-free.app/api/webhooks/clerk
```

Replace with your ngrok URL.

---

## Step 5: Select Events

Enable:

```text
user.created
user.updated
organization.created
organizationMembership.created
organizationMembership.deleted
```

Click **Create**.

---

## Step 6: Copy Signing Secret

After creating the webhook, Clerk will show:

```text
Webhook Secret
```

Example:

```text
whsec_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
```

Add it to your `.env`:

```env
CLERK_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
```

---

## Step 7: Create Express Route

Example:

```javascript
import express from "express";

const router = express.Router();

router.post("/clerk", async (req, res) => {
  console.log("Webhook Received");
  console.log(req.body);

  res.status(200).json({ success: true });
});

export default router;
```

Register it:

```javascript
app.use("/api/webhooks", webhookRoutes);
```

---

